From f7fa6e2a059d371fcb0c675e5721169bdfcd6bd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bourgois <karel@voxist.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 18:28:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(beads): gc owns the proxied db-proxy lifecycle
 (never-idle + reap on stop)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When [beads] proxied is on, gascity now owns the db-proxy lifecycle end to
end instead of leaving each db-proxy-child to idle-die and respawn on its own
clock (Option 2). Two changes:

- Default proxy_idle_timeout to "0" (never idle). Any finite timeout is
  starved by sparse controller probes, producing spawn/serve/idle-die/respawn
  churn that never reaches the warm-pool steady state. A never-idle proxy stays
  warm for the city's lifetime; a crash at worst leaves a still-usable warm
  proxy that the next stop reaps.

- Reap the proxies on genuine  (reapProxiedChildrenForCity, wired into
  stopManagedDoltProcessWithOptions on the clearPublishedState path). Discovery
  is by live process table matched on the db-proxy-child --root under each
  scope's .beads, never by pidfile — a stale pidfile must not make us signal an
  unrelated PID.

Pairs with the bd-side fix that stops the proxy's ephemeral port from being
written into .beads/dolt-server.port; together they make dolt-server.port a
single-owner artifact (gc writes the managed port; bd never clobbers it).
